  "source": {
    "type": "hadith",
    "references": ["Sahih al-Bukhari 2363", "Sahih al-Bukhari 2466", "Sahih Muslim 2244"],
    "summary": "A man travelling became very thirsty, found a well, went down into it and drank. When he came out he saw a dog panting and licking the moist earth out of thirst. He said: this dog has become as thirsty as I was. He went down again, filled his leather sock (khuff) with water, held it with his mouth, climbed up and gave the dog water. Allah appreciated his deed and forgave him. The Companions asked: is there a reward for us in (serving) animals? He said: there is a reward for (serving) every living being.",
    "verified": false
  },
